 {
  "path": "plugins/comment-review/skills/comment-review/scripts/galley.py",
  "start": 1,
  "end": 35,
  "kind": "docstring",
  "lines": 35,
  "text": "The proposed text, SET AS FILES, so it can be read and censused like any tree. python galley.py --repo D --census census.json --edits edits.json --out DIR A galley is the trial impression: the text set, but not yet made into pages, so that it can be corrected before anything is committed. That is exactly what this writes -- every block a stage proposes to change, spliced into a copy of its file under `--out`. Nothing under `--repo` is touched. !! IT RENDERS; IT DOES NOT RULE. A stage that both produced the galley and judged it would be MARK and APPLY in one actor, which is the separation the pipeline exists to keep. Two things need it, and they needed the same thing: round 2 A re-review rules on the SYNTHESISED block -- text on no disk and in no census -- so `address_problem` refuses it and `edit_problem` measures one claim against one edit where the block now holds several. Censusing the galley gives that text a real address, so every check in `verdicts.py` works on it UNCHANGED. The alternatives were a second record shape to hold in sync, or a flag that turns the checks off for the one text the author actually approves. stage 7a What lands at 7b is a block spliced into a file, and the splice is the first time anyone sees the two together. `git diff --no-index` over the galley WOULD show the author what will land, including whether an adjacent block was clipped -- which a `CHANGE` cannot show, because each one carries its own surrounding context. ! Stage 7a does not set a galley today; it presents the blocks inline. This is the second caller the module was built for and it is not wired. ! A SPLICE THAT CANNOT BE MADE IS REPORTED, NEVER GUESSED. A census range that no longer matches the file, or two edits over one line, stops that file rather than writing a galley nobody can trust.",
  "anchor": "<module>",
  "tier": "tokenized",
  "annotations": [
   "cites-a-path",
   "forbids-a-literal",
   "names-a-symbol",
   "narrative-in-docstring"
  ],
  "notes": [
   "UNRESOLVED symbol `address_problem` (CANDIDATE)",
   "UNRESOLVED symbol `edit_problem` (CANDIDATE)",
   "UNRESOLVED symbol `verdicts.py` (CANDIDATE)",
   "UNRESOLVED symbol `CHANGE` (CANDIDATE)",
   "UNRESOLVED path census.json",
   "UNRESOLVED path edits.json",
   "UNRESOLVED path verdicts.py",
   "GREP this file for what it forbids: 'no disk and in no census -- so `address_problem`'",
   "a review label: round 2   A re-review rules on the SYNTHESISED block -- text",
   "a retraction: no longer matches the file, or two edits over one line, stop"
  ],
  "raw_lines": [
   "\"\"\"The proposed text, SET AS FILES, so it can be read and censused like any tree.",
   "",
   "    python galley.py --repo D --census census.json --edits edits.json --out DIR",
   "",
   "A galley is the trial impression: the text set, but not yet made into pages, so",
   "that it can be corrected before anything is committed. That is exactly what",
   "this writes -- every block a stage proposes to change, spliced into a copy of",
   "its file under `--out`. Nothing under `--repo` is touched.",
   "",
   "!! IT RENDERS; IT DOES NOT RULE. A stage that both produced the galley and",
   "judged it would be MARK and APPLY in one actor, which is the separation the",
   "pipeline exists to keep.",
   "",
   "Two things need it, and they needed the same thing:",
   "",
   "  round 2   A re-review rules on the SYNTHESISED block -- text on no disk and",
   "            in no census -- so `address_problem` refuses it and `edit_problem`",
   "            measures one claim against one edit where the block now holds",
   "            several. Censusing the galley gives that text a real address, so",
   "            every check in `verdicts.py` works on it UNCHANGED. The",
   "            alternatives were a second record shape to hold in sync, or a flag",
   "            that turns the checks off for the one text the author actually",
   "            approves.",
   "  stage 7a  What lands at 7b is a block spliced into a file, and the splice is",
   "            the first time anyone sees the two together. `git diff --no-index`",
   "            over the galley WOULD show the author what will land, including",
   "            whether an adjacent block was clipped -- which a `CHANGE` cannot",
   "            show, because each one carries its own surrounding context. ! Stage",
   "            7a does not set a galley today; it presents the blocks inline. This",
   "            is the second caller the module was built for and it is not wired.",
   "",
   "! A SPLICE THAT CANNOT BE MADE IS REPORTED, NEVER GUESSED. A census range that",
   "no longer matches the file, or two edits over one line, stops that file rather",
   "than writing a galley nobody can trust.",
   "\"\"\""
  ]
